# src/apps/daemon/internal/runtime/runtimecore

## Purpose
Long-lived daemon runtime-engine owner for Tor/Psiphon lifecycle and status; intentionally separate from temporary proxy qualification cores.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `runtime` (rank 4; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (17): `adapters.go`, `adapters_transport_test.go`, `capability.go`, `capability_test.go`, `chaining_test.go`, `engine_lifecycle_unix_test.go`, `ikev2_engine.go`, `ikev2_engine_test.go`, `integration_unix_test.go`, `ipsec_manager.go`, `ipsec_manager_test.go`, `manager.go` …

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `runtimecore`.
- Notable exported surface: `Capability`, `DefaultIkev2Proposal`, `DefaultManager`, `Engine`, `ErrInvalidRequest`, `Ikev2Proposal`, `IpsecProfile`, `Manager`, `NatTKeepaliveDaemon`, `NewIpsecProfile` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/flowregistry`, `internal/platform/process`, `internal/platform/system`.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`, `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/adapters/mobilebind`.

## Invariants
- Tor/Psiphon are long-lived daemon-owned runtime adapters.
- Runtime engine lifetime is started/stopped/joined by daemon lifetime, never HTTP request lifetime.
- `runtime` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
